# Interface definition for thorn MCNuX

IMPLEMENTS: MCNuX

# The geodesic push of specs/geodesic-propagation.md reads the ADMBaseX
# metric, lapse, and shift grid functions, and the fluid-state gather of
# specs/neutrino-matter-interactions.md reads the HydroBaseX (rho, vel,
# temperature, Ye) grid functions (READS: clauses in schedule.ccl);
# the CST accepts a READS: on another implementation's variables only through
# an INHERITS: (a bare cross-thorn READS: is a CST error: "No access to
# variable ... Maybe add an inherits clause"). This is read access to the
# published spacetime/fluid interfaces only — no dependence on any evolution
# thorn (GRMHD-/spacetime-agnosticism of specs/build-and-integration.md is
# kept: ADMBaseX and HydroBaseX are the data-declaring base thorns, not
# evolvers; the sibling precedent is TestMCNuX/interface.ccl).
INHERITS: ADMBaseX HydroBaseX

USES INCLUDE HEADER: loop_device.hxx

# Transport-cadence diagnostics of specs/carpetx-thorn-integration.md
# [MCNX-CTX-05]. The counter is an MCNuX-owned grid scalar (no INHERITS is
# needed: MCNuX both reads and writes its own variable), so that the routines
# of the transport-step group carry real READS:/WRITES: clauses and the
# driver's validity machinery enforces [MCNX-CTX-04] at runtime. The counter
# is the "transport-step counter" the cadence benchmark of
# specs/verification-suite-design.md later consumes as a per-iteration norm.
# It is checkpointed (the default): the count is part of the transport state,
# so a recovered run must continue the same sequence.

CCTK_INT mcnux_transport_diag TYPE=SCALAR
{
  transport_step_count
} "MCNuX transport-cadence diagnostics (number of completed transport steps)"

# Result table of the unit self-test battery, specs/verification-suite-design.md
# [MCNX-VER-01]/[MCNX-VER-06]: "one row per named check (measured error, pass
# flag)". A 1d grid array with one element per check is exactly that shape —
# CarpetX's WriteTSVArrays emits one TSV line per array index, so the golden
# file is literally the table of rows. DISTRIB=CONSTANT because the battery is
# a global, rank-independent computation (every test runs NPROCS 1 anyway).
#
# The index -> name mapping is owned by, and documented in,
# src/mcnux_selftest.cxx; that table is append-only, so SIZE grows (and the
# golden data is regenerated) whenever a later task adds checks. The routine
# cross-checks SIZE against its own table length at runtime, so the two cannot
# drift silently.
#
# Not checkpointed: the battery is recomputed from nothing but code, so it is
# not part of any evolved state.

CCTK_REAL mcnux_selftest TYPE=ARRAY DIM=1 SIZE=166 DISTRIB=CONSTANT TAGS='checkpoint="no"'
{
  selftest_error
  selftest_pass
} "MCNuX unit self-test battery results (measured error and pass flag per check)"

# Per-packet diagnostic table of the synthetic packet fixture
# (specs/geodesic-propagation.md, Verification: flat-spacetime exactness and
# Schwarzschild p_t conservation; the `minkowski-freestream` benchmark).
# CarpetX has no particle TSV writer, so the packet state is mirrored into a
# 1d grid array with one row per fixture packet (row = packet id - 1, hence
# independent of tile and iteration order): position x^i, lower momentum
# p_i, and the covariant energy p_t = -alpha^2 p^t + beta^i p_i
# (geodesic-propagation.md:121-123), which is -|p| on Minkowski and the
# conserved quantity of the later Schwarzschild benchmark. SIZE is the
# fixture count of src/mcnux_geodesic.cxx, cross-checked at runtime.
# Storage is parameter-gated (schedule.ccl); not checkpointed: the table is
# recomputed from the population after every push.

CCTK_REAL mcnux_packet_diag TYPE=ARRAY DIM=1 SIZE=8 DISTRIB=CONSTANT TAGS='checkpoint="no"'
{
  pk_x pk_y pk_z pk_px pk_py pk_pz pk_pt
} "MCNuX synthetic packet diagnostics (position, lower momentum, covariant energy per fixture packet)"

# Per-packet emission-identity diagnostic table
# (specs/packet-representation-and-sampling.md [MCNX-PKT-01/02/03/05]; the
# `emission-fixedseed` benchmark of specs/verification-suite-design.md:243,
# "exact packet set (ids, states) golden"). Sibling of mcnux_packet_diag:
# the discrete half of the created packet state — AMReX id, weight
# N = E_p/nu, species index (0 nu_e, 1 nu_e_bar, 2 nu_x), and the RNG event
# counter e — all integers or exact binary fractions stored exactly in
# binary64. Same row keying as mcnux_packet_diag: row = packet id - 1
# (independent of tile and iteration order), zero rows for unissued ids, and
# the same SIZE-cap discipline: a packet id above SIZE is a hard CCTK_VERROR
# (the id budget of the benchmark tuning, never a silent truncation). SIZE
# is cross-checked at runtime against the fill routine's bound. A SEPARATE
# group (not extra mcnux_packet_diag columns) so every existing benchmark's
# per-group golden TSVs stay byte-stable. Storage is parameter-gated
# (schedule.ccl); not checkpointed: recomputed from the population every
# fill.

CCTK_REAL mcnux_emission_diag TYPE=ARRAY DIM=1 SIZE=8 DISTRIB=CONSTANT TAGS='checkpoint="no"'
{
  em_id em_w em_species em_ec
} "MCNuX per-packet emission identity diagnostics (AMReX id, weight, species index, event counter per created packet)"

# Per-packet fluid-gather diagnostic table
# (specs/neutrino-matter-interactions.md [MCNX-INT-05] and its inputs table:
# the cell-centered (rho, T[MeV], Ye) fluid state of the packet's containing
# cell, read verbatim with no sub-cell interpolation, plus the cell-centered
# fluid four-velocity u^mu from the Valencia lift of mcnux_fluid.hxx; the
# `hydro-sphere-gather` benchmark golden-checks it against the closed-form
# TestMCNuX profile). Same shape and row keying as mcnux_packet_diag: one row
# per fixture packet (row = packet id - 1), SIZE cross-checked at runtime.
# Storage is parameter-gated (schedule.ccl); not checkpointed: the table is
# recomputed from the population and the fluid state every fill.

CCTK_REAL mcnux_fluid_diag TYPE=ARRAY DIM=1 SIZE=8 DISTRIB=CONSTANT TAGS='checkpoint="no"'
{
  fl_rho fl_temp fl_ye fl_u0 fl_u1 fl_u2 fl_u3
} "MCNuX per-packet gathered fluid state (rho [g/cm^3], T [MeV], Ye) and cell-centered four-velocity u^mu"

# Conservation-ledger closure diagnostic table
# (specs/hydro-coupling-source-terms.md [MCNX-HYD-05]; the closure observable
# of the `source-zero-add` benchmark): one row per channel X in
# {P^t, P_x, P_y, P_z, L} (row = channel index in that order), columns the
# grid total Sum_cells (source value)*dV*dt, the event-side net dX_packets,
# the gross event activity Sum_events |dX| (the closure denominator), the
# residual |grid + net|, and the pass flag of
#   residual <= 1e-13 * max(gross, eps0)
# (ledger_rtol/ledger_eps0 of src/mcnux_srcterms.hxx, where the eps0 floor is
# documented). Same shape idiom as mcnux_packet_diag/mcnux_fluid_diag;
# storage is parameter-gated (schedule.ccl); not checkpointed: the table is
# recomputed from the source variables and the synthetic event list every
# fill.

CCTK_REAL mcnux_ledger_diag TYPE=ARRAY DIM=1 SIZE=5 DISTRIB=CONSTANT TAGS='checkpoint="no"'
{
  lg_grid_total lg_event_net lg_gross lg_residual lg_pass
} "MCNuX conservation-ledger closure diagnostics (grid total, event net, gross activity, residual, pass per channel P^t, P_x, P_y, P_z, L)"

# Statistical-check verdict table of specs/verification-suite-design.md
# [MCNX-VER-07] (the binding per-check output shape: estimate, expected value,
# standard error sigma, and z = (estimate - expected)/sigma) — the output of
# the stats-tier writers, first consumer MCNuX_StatsEmission (the
# `stats-emission` benchmark, [MCNX-PKT-06]). One row per check; the
# stats-emission row layout (4 rows per species in species_index order:
# count, energy, cos(theta) mean, phi mean; then the two RNG uniformity rows)
# is owned by, and documented in, src/mcnux_emission.cxx, which cross-checks
# SIZE against its own row count at runtime. Acceptance |z| <= 4 is judged
# once at golden capture; thereafter the archived z values are golden numbers
# diffed at 1e-12. Same shape idiom as mcnux_ledger_diag; storage is
# parameter-gated (schedule.ccl); not checkpointed: the table is recomputed
# from the per-step accumulator every fill.

CCTK_REAL mcnux_stats_diag TYPE=ARRAY DIM=1 SIZE=14 DISTRIB=CONSTANT TAGS='checkpoint="no"'
{
  stats_estimate stats_expected stats_sigma stats_z
} "MCNuX statistical-check verdicts (estimate, expected, standard error, standardized deviation z per check)"

# Per-species escape-tally diagnostic table
# (specs/particle-container-and-gpu.md [MCNX-GPU-05]: packets that leave the
# outer domain boundary are removed and TALLIED as escapes, never silently
# dropped; the `escape-freestream` benchmark). Species-major layout, row =
# escape_slot(species, channel) = 3 * species + channel of
# src/mcnux_escape.hxx: 3 species (0 nu_e, 1 nu_e_bar, 2 nu_x) x
# {escaped-packet count, escaped number Sum N, escaped energy Sum N p^t with
# p^t the upper-index null-closure energy on the last-in-domain metric — the
# ledger energy convention, NOT the covariant pk_pt column}. The values are
# the RUN-CUMULATIVE totals of the TU-owned accumulator behind
# escape_run_tally() (mcnux_escape.cxx), mirrored each transport step;
# detection/tally/removal at the push and episode-driver sites is ALWAYS ON —
# only this table is parameter-gated (schedule.ccl, test_escape_tallies).
# SIZE is cross-checked at runtime against escape_num_slots. Not
# checkpointed (the mcnux_*_diag convention); the accumulator's restart
# persistence is a recorded deferred limitation (src/mcnux_escape.hxx).

CCTK_REAL mcnux_escape_diag TYPE=ARRAY DIM=1 SIZE=9 DISTRIB=CONSTANT TAGS='checkpoint="no"'
{
  esc_tally
} "MCNuX run-cumulative per-species escape tallies (packet count, number, energy per species, species-major)"

# MCNuX-owned source-term grid variables of
# specs/hydro-coupling-source-terms.md [MCNX-HYD-01] — the published coupling
# interface a GRMHD partner's READS: clauses reference ([MCNX-HYD-04]), hence
# PUBLIC. Cell-centered (CENTERING={ccc}, matching HydroBaseX), geometrized
# code units, per unit coordinate volume per unit coordinate time,
# undensitized (no sqrt(gamma) folded in). Sign convention: POSITIVE = GAINED
# BY THE FLUID ([MCNX-HYD-02]: G = -Delta P/(dV dt), S_l = -Delta L/(dV dt) —
# what packets gain, the fluid loses). Checkpointed: the values tallied at
# step n are read by the fluid at step n+1, so they carry state across steps
# and a checkpoint/recovery cycle between transport and the partner's read
# must not alter what the partner reads ([MCNX-HYD-01]).

PUBLIC:

CCTK_REAL rad_force TYPE=gf CENTERING={ccc} TAGS='checkpoint="yes"'
{
  rf_t rf_x rf_y rf_z
} "Radiation four-force density on the fluid: G^t (index up) and G_x, G_y, G_z (index down)"

CCTK_REAL lepton_source TYPE=gf CENTERING={ccc} TAGS='checkpoint="yes"'
{
  lep_src
} "Net electron-lepton number source density to the fluid"
